    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The suite consists of the two acceptance tests, both green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` derivation following the exact pattern the codebase already uses for `membershipTier`, keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New `Locality` helper** (`model/Locality.java`) \u2014 a tiny, cohesive class with a fixed city\u2192region map and a single static `of(city)` that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. It has near-zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other \u2248 0), so it's the cheapest place to hold the new behaviour.\n\n2. **One mapper line** (`OwnerMapper.java`) \u2014 added a single `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", \u2026)` expression alongside the existing `membershipTier` mapping. The mapper's other methods are all CC 1, so this change is cheap.\n\n3. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added the `locality` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nNo existing method was grown, and no code was added to the large `Owner` class. The cost is dominated by two trivial edits (a one-line mapper annotation and a schema block) plus one small new file.",
